          "filename": "St. Mary's Church, Haddington, East Lothian, Scotland. - geograph.org.uk - 658100.jpg",
          "caption": "St. Mary's Church, Haddington, East Lothian, Scotland. in the late 12th century a Franciscan Abbey was built near this site. Destroyed by an English attack across East Lothian, known as \"The Burnt Candlemas\" St Mary's, from 14th-15th centuries, has suffered many times at the hands of the English. Fully restored in the 1970s. Photograph taken from Nungate Bridge.",
